<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">István Werbőczy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1458–<a href="/years/1541">1541</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Stephen Werbőczy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">István Werbőczy was a Hungarian jurist and politician who compiled the customary law of the Hungarian nobility in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartitum">Tripartitum</a>, presented to the diet in 1514. A leader of the lesser nobility, he briefly served as palatine in 1525 and was later appointed chief judge of the Hungarians in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. His code entrenched noble privilege and remained the basis of Hungarian law until 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/istvan-werboczy.jpg" alt="István Werbőczy" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Verb%C5%91czy_Istv%C3%A1n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under the Jagiellonian kings Vladislaus II and Louis II the great magnates regained control and royal revenues collapsed, while the lawyer <b>István Werbőczy</b> compiled the customary law of the nobility in the Tripartitum of 1514, which remained the basis of Hungarian noble law until 1848.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Verbovets', in what is now <a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.17,22.91&amp;year=1511" aria-label="Verbovets' on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5083 478 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of István Werbőczy"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5533 748h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5533 748h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.17,22.91&amp;year=1511">What was here in 1511? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
